# UI/UX & Styling Guidelines

## Design System
- **Component Library**: shadcn/ui (see [components.json](mdc:components.json) for configuration)
- **Styling**: Tailwind CSS 4 with custom configuration
- **Icons**: Lucide React icons
- **Animations**: tw-animate-css for enhanced animations

## Component Architecture
- Use shadcn/ui components as base building blocks
- Customize components using Tailwind utilities and CSS variables
- Create compound components for complex UI patterns
- Implement proper accessibility (ARIA labels, keyboard navigation)

## Styling Patterns
- Use Tailwind utility classes for styling
- Leverage CSS variables for theming (dark/light mode ready)
- Use `clsx` and `tailwind-merge` for conditional classes
- Implement responsive design with Tailwind breakpoints

## Chat UI Specifications
- **Message List**: Reverse chronological with auto-scroll to bottom
- **Message Bubbles**: Different styles for sent/received messages
- **Typing Indicators**: Animated dots with user avatars
- **Presence Status**: Online/away indicators with colored dots
- **Image Messages**: Thumbnails with full-screen preview on tap

## Form Patterns
- Use proper form validation with inline error messages
- Implement loading states with disabled buttons and spinners
- Show toast notifications for success/error feedback
- Use proper focus management and accessibility

## Layout Components
- **Navigation**: Clean header with user profile and logout
- **Sidebar**: Chat list with unread counts and search
- **Main Content**: Chat interface with message composer
- **Modals**: Profile editing, group creation, settings

## Responsive Design
- Mobile-first approach with progressive enhancement
- Touch-friendly interface elements (44px minimum touch targets)
- Proper spacing and typography scales
- Optimized for both mobile and desktop experiences

## Performance Considerations
- Use proper image optimization with Next.js Image component
- Implement virtualization for long message lists
- Use CSS transforms for smooth animations
- Minimize layout shifts with proper sizing

## Accessibility Standards
- Proper semantic HTML structure
- ARIA labels and roles for interactive elements
- Keyboard navigation support
- Screen reader compatibility
- High contrast mode support